pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% POSITIVE CONTROL for the `solx` empty-preserved-set fix: refusing an EMPTY preserved set must
% not touch a preserved set of size one. Both values of x1 extend to a solution, so the complete
% enumeration over the preserved set is 2, and the two exclusions contradict each other.
f 1;
solx x1 x2;
solx ~x1 x2;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE 2;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
